// =====================================================================
// Aurora Pharma cold chain — 03. THE MATERIALIZED VIEW
//
// This is the always-fresh, engine-maintained running total of every batch's
// exposure. It is the single source of truth for the aggregate, and it exists
// because the platform maintains it better than a job can.
//
// Microsoft's own description (materialized-view-overview, ms.date 2024-08-11):
//   "Materialized views always return an up-to-date result of the aggregation
//    query (always fresh)."
//   "A materialized view query always returns the most up-to-date results,
//    independent of when materialization last took place. The query combines
//    the materialized part of the view with the records in the source table,
//    which haven't yet been materialized (the delta part)."
//   "Querying a materialized view consumes less resources than doing the
//    aggregation over the source table."
//
// WHY THE AGGREGATION IS THIS SIMPLE. A materialized view can aggregate over
// exactly one source table, so it cannot join leg_cargo for the budget
// denominator. The update policy in 02 solved that at ingestion time by
// computing each reading's BudgetPctIncrement while it already had the budget
// in hand. Summing those increments is arithmetically identical to dividing
// the total by the budget, so the view stays a pure aggregation and the engine
// can maintain it incrementally.
//
// Run once, after 02-enrichment.kql.
// =====================================================================

// backfill=true builds the view over data already in excursion_events. Leave it
// out and the view only covers rows ingested from this moment on, which is a
// quiet way to lose your whole seed.
.create materialized-view with (backfill=true, docstring="Running cold-chain exposure per drug batch across every leg of its journey. Always fresh. Bound to the Batch entity as a timeseries property.")
BatchExposureMV on table excursion_events
{
    excursion_events
    | summarize
        CumulativeMinutes = sum(ExcursionMinutes),
        // The sum of per-reading shares. Identical to
        // 100 * CumulativeMinutes / BudgetMinutes, but expressible without a join.
        BudgetUsedPct     = sum(BudgetPctIncrement),
        // Counted, never budgeted. A frozen vial is destroyed, so there is no
        // such thing as "8% of your freeze allowance used". Its own column
        // means it can have its own rule, which matters because the operations
        // agent does not support AND conditions.
        FreezeEventCount  = countif(Direction == "cold" and ExcursionMinutes > 0),
        BudgetMinutes     = max(BudgetMinutes),
        LastReading       = max(Timestamp)
      by BatchID
}

// Confirm it built and is healthy. Watch IsHealthy and the materialized-to
// watermark; a view that stops advancing is a silent outage.
.show materialized-view BatchExposureMV
.show materialized-view BatchExposureMV failures

// Read it exactly as you would a table.
BatchExposureMV
| order by BudgetUsedPct desc
| take 20
